\import{base-macros}
\author{kellenkanarios}
\title{Entropy is concave}
\taxon{Theorem}
\tag{public}

\p{[Entropy](0081) is a concave functional of the distribution: for #{\lambda\in[0,1]},
##{H(\lambda P_1+(1-\lambda)P_2)\ \geq\ \lambda H(P_1)+(1-\lambda)H(P_2).}
Mixing two distributions never destroys uncertainty — the entropy of a mixture is at least the mixture of entropies.}

\p{This is the mirror image of [[WV2P]]. Writing #{H(P)=\log|\mathcal{X}|-D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\,\|\,U)} against the uniform law #{U}, concavity of #{H} is exactly convexity of #{P\mapsto D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P\|U)}. Concavity is what makes the maximum in [[6FHG]] well-behaved — a concave objective on the simplex has a unique maximizer.}
